<title>FINLAND: Kesko extends losses on disposal plan.</title>
<headline>Kesko extends losses on disposal plan.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1996-10-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Finnish wholesaler Kesko Oy extended losses in fair trade on Tuesday on investors' disappointment with its plans to sell parts of Tuko to gain the EU's approval for its merger with the group, brokers said.</p>
<p>At 1325 GMT, Kesko traded at 69.60 markka, its lowest since August 7, down 2.90 markka or four percent. Trade was a fair 7.3 million markka.</p>
<p>Brokers saw scope for further losses in Kesko since an overall sharp fall on the Helsinki bourse put additional pressure on the share.</p>
<p>-- Helsinki newsroom +358-9-6805 0245</p>
